{"classified_as":[{"_id":"http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300033799","label":"oil paintings (visual works)","type":"Type"},{"_id":"http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300033618","label":"paintings (visual works)","type":"Type"},{"_label":"Collection Item","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404024","type":"Type"}],"id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/object/8762","identified_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"repository number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404621"}],"content":"8762","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"non-preferred identifiers","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300264273"}],"content":"718, Catalogue Raisonné","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"catalogue raisonnée number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026061"}],"content":"718","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"preferred term","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404670"}],"content":"Jack-in-the-Pulpit No. IV","type":"Name"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"non-preferred identifiers","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300264273"}],"content":{"alternate-title-1999-catalogue-raisonne":{"titles":[{"notes":"Source of title: Whitney Archive.","title":"No 6 Jack-in-the-Pulpit","type":"alternate-title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"},{"notes":"Source of title: Whitney Archive.","title":"Jack-in-the-Pulpit","type":"alternate-title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"},{"notes":"Source of title: Whitney Archive.","title":"Jack-in-the-Pulpit, No. 4","type":"alternate-title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"},{"notes":"Source of title: Downtown Gallery label.","title":"Jack-in-the-Pulpit #6","type":"alternate-title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"}],"type":"alternate-title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"},"selected-exhibition-titles":{"titles":["Jack in the Pulpit IV\nGeorgia O'Keeffe: The Poetry of Things, 1999, Georgia O'Keeffe Museum (Santa Fe)"],"type":"selected-exhibition-titles"},"title-1999-catalogue-raisonne":{"titles":[{"notes":"Source of title: Downtown Gallery Archive, Abiquiú Notebooks.","title":"Jack-in-the-Pulpit No. IV","type":"title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"}],"type":"title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"}},"type":"Name"}],"produced_by":{"carried_out_by":[{"_label":"Georgia O'Keeffe","id":"actor/2","type":"Actor"}],"timespan":{"type":"TimeSpan"},"type":"Production"},"referred_to_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Complete","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_complete"}],"content":"Georgia O'Keeffe. Jack-in-the-Pulpit No. IV, 1930. Oil on canvas, 40 x 30 inches. National Gallery of Art (NGA). National Gallery of Art, Washington, Alfred Stieglitz Collection, Bequest of Georgia O'Keeffe, 1987.58.3. © Board of Trustees, National Gallery of Art, Washington","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Holding Institution","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_instituion"}],"content":"National Gallery of Art (NGA)","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"description statement","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"}],"content":"The smooth, velvety black spathe of a jack-in-the-pulpit surrounds the plant's deep blue spadix. A single white vein extends along the spathe, expanding where it meets the spadix and framing it like a glowing halo. Behind the plant are several overlapping green leaves and a softly shaded blue background.","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"provenance_narrative","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/provenance_narrative"}],"content":"The artist; by exchange 1955 through (Downtown Gallery, New York) to Drs. Melvin [1920-1969] and Helen W. [1921-2009] Boigon, New York, until at least 1971;[1] sold 1972 through (Hirschl \u0026 Adler Galleries, Inc., New York) to private collection, Miami; (Kennedy Galleries, Inc., New York), in 1973; returned 1973 through Doris Bry, New York, to the artist [1887-1986];[2] her estate; bequest 1987 to NGA. \n (Source: NGA, 2025) \n \n \n[1] The artist wrote to Edith Halpert, owner of the Downtown Gallery, on 3 January 1955: \"The Boigons write me that they have exchanged the Antelope [Pedernal] for the \"Jack In The Pulpit\" -- and I don't know which one.\" Halpert responded on 8 January 1955: \"Yes, the Boigons decided to exchange 'Antelope and Pedernal' for the large 'Jack-in-the-Pulpit #6' date 1930.\" (The letters are in the Downtown Gallery Records, 1824-1974, Archives of American Art, Smithsonian Institution, Washington:  Artist Files, A-Z: O'Keeffe, Georgia 1951-1955, Box 25, Reel 5550, Frames 1173-1175 and 1177-1178; copies in NGA curatorial files.) The artist and Doris Bry renumbered the Jack-in-the-Pulpit series in 1970; this painting, now the fourth, was originally the sixth. \n \n[2] The provenance is from Lynes, 1999","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"cr_remarks_1999","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/cr_remarks_1999"}],"content":["Backing inscription 1 indicates \"No. 6.\" Exhibited in 1943 as No. 4 and titled as such with minor variations in Whitney Archive, Downtown Gallery Archive, Abiquiú Notebooks and label printed by O'Keeffe (white). Exchanged in 1954 for cat. no. 1264. \"Yes, the Boigons decided to exchange 'Antelope and Pedernal' [cat. no. 1264] for the large 'Jack–in–the–Pulpit #6' date 1930. It is 30 x 40. . . . it is now being sprayed by Mrs. Keck\" (Edith Halpert to O'Keeffe, 8 January 1955, Archive of American Art). Series renumbered by O'Keeffe and Doris Bry in 1970. Pictured in 1931 New York (An American Place) Stieglitz installation photographs, see Appendix III, figures 44, 45. (Source: Lynes, 1999)"],"type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Measurement Description","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/measurement_description"}],"content":"40 x 30 inches","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Copyright","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_copyright"}],"content":"© Board of Trustees, National Gallery of Art, Washington","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Artist(s)","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_artist"}],"content":"Georgia O'Keeffe","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Medium and Dimensions","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_medium_dims"}],"content":"Oil on canvas, 40 x 30 inches","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Title and Date","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_title_date"}],"content":"Jack-in-the-Pulpit No. IV, 1930","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"credit line","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026687"}],"content":"National Gallery of Art, Washington, Alfred Stieglitz Collection, Bequest of Georgia O'Keeffe, 1987.58.3","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Materials description","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/materials_description"}],"content":"Oil on canvas","type":"LinguisticObject"}],"representation":[{"digitally_shown_by":[{"access_point":[{"id":"https://iiif.okeeffemuseum.org/image/iiif/2/857687/full/full/0/default.jpg","type":"DigitalObject"}],"classified_as":[{"_label":"Digital Image","id":"http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300215302","type":"Type"}],"digitally_available_via":[{"access_point":[{"id":"https://iiif.okeeffemuseum.org/image/iiif/2/857687"}],"conforms_to":[{"id":"http://iiif.io/api/image","type":"InformationObject"}],"format":"application/ld+json;profile='http://iiif.io/api/image/2/context.json'","type":"DigitalService"}],"type":"DigitalObject"}],"type":"VisualItem"}],"type":"HumanMadeObject"}